WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.133
-The January 6th Committee

00:00:03.133 --> 00:00:04.667
revealed a series
of depositions today

00:00:04.667 --> 00:00:06.434
from former aides
to President Trump,

00:00:06.434 --> 00:00:09.601
who said he was watching TV
as the insurrection unfolded.

00:00:09.601 --> 00:00:12.400
Meanwhile, the Secret Service
has mysteriously deleted

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.634
text messages from
the day of the coup attempt,

00:00:14.634 --> 00:00:17.601
despite requests from Congress
to preserve all records

00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:19.033
related to January 6th.

00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:21.467
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:21.467 --> 00:00:23.467
[ Theme music plays ]

00:00:23.467 --> 00:00:25.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:25.501 --> 00:00:28.534
The January 6th Committee
was back in prime time tonight,

00:00:28.534 --> 00:00:30.167
which means
we don't know what happened,

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:31.901
because we taped this
before the hearing.

00:00:31.901 --> 00:00:35.501
Although, given how shocking
the previous hearings have been,

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:37.434
I'm not taking anything
off the table.

00:00:37.434 --> 00:00:39.601
Maybe you're watching this
right now thinking, "Oh, my God,

00:00:39.601 --> 00:00:42.467
I can't believe Trump tried
to commandeer Air Force One

00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:44.968
so he could fly to the Capitol,
but then got lost

00:00:44.968 --> 00:00:46.601
and crashed
in the Atlantic Ocean,

00:00:46.601 --> 00:00:48.534
where he was adrift at sea
for several weeks

00:00:48.534 --> 00:00:50.834
and befriended a volley ball
he named Mike Pence."

00:00:50.834 --> 00:00:52.000
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.601
In fairness,
if you saw a volleyball,

00:00:54.601 --> 00:00:57.167
you could definitely be forgiven
for thinking it was Mike Pence.

00:00:57.167 --> 00:00:58.501
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.501 --> 00:01:00.467
Or maybe you're sitting at home
right now, thinking,

00:01:00.467 --> 00:01:02.033
"I can't believe
Rudy Giuliani..."

00:01:02.033 --> 00:01:04.133
Actually, you know what?
Never mind.

00:01:04.133 --> 00:01:07.701
Shame on all of us
if we're ever surprised again

00:01:07.701 --> 00:01:10.100
by anything Rudy does
from this point forward.

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:12.200
I mean, he already
leaked hair dye

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:15.334
on national television and
posted a video on Twitter

00:01:15.334 --> 00:01:17.367
with his shorts
down to his ankles,

00:01:17.367 --> 00:01:20.267
swinging a golf club
back and forth

00:01:20.267 --> 00:01:22.200
like the world's
[bleep] hypnotist.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:25.267
"You're getting very sleepy,
and so am I.

00:01:25.267 --> 00:01:28.100
Good thing I'm already wearing
my pajama shorts."

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:29.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:31.100
So, as we're taping this,
we don't know

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:32.400
exactly what happened,

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:35.000
but the committee did release
an early teaser today --

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.167
a series of depositions
with former Trump aides

00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:40.167
who all testified that as
the seat of our government

00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:41.968
was under attack
by a violent mob,

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:45.667
Trump himself incited, as part
of a carefully orchestrated plot

00:01:45.667 --> 00:01:47.267
to overthrow American democracy,

00:01:47.267 --> 00:01:50.267
Trump was doing one thing,
and one thing only --

00:01:50.267 --> 00:01:53.434
sitting in the White House
dining room, watching TV.

00:01:53.434 --> 00:01:56.267
-Was the President
in that private dining room

00:01:56.267 --> 00:01:59.567
the whole time that the attack
on the Capitol was going on?

00:01:59.567 --> 00:02:02.968
Or did he ever go --
again, only to your knowledge --

00:02:02.968 --> 00:02:04.367
to the Oval Office,

00:02:04.367 --> 00:02:07.467
to the White House
Situation Room, anywhere else?

00:02:07.467 --> 00:02:09.300
-To the best
of my recollection,

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:11.000
he was always
in the dining room.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:14.767
-What did they say, Mr. Meadows
or the President, at all,

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:16.868
during that brief encounter that
you were in the dining room?

00:02:16.868 --> 00:02:17.901
What do you recall?
-I think they --

00:02:17.901 --> 00:02:19.667
everyone was watching the TV.

00:02:19.667 --> 00:02:23.067
-Do you know whether he was
watching TV in the dining room

00:02:23.067 --> 00:02:25.501
when you talked to him
on January 6?

00:02:25.501 --> 00:02:31.033
-It's my understanding he
was watching television.

00:02:31.033 --> 00:02:32.567
-When you were
in the dining room

00:02:32.567 --> 00:02:37.367
in these discussions,
was the violence at the Capitol

00:02:37.367 --> 00:02:40.801
visible on the screen?
On the television?

00:02:40.801 --> 00:02:42.367
-Yes. Right.

00:02:42.367 --> 00:02:43.701
-You got to
give it to Donald Trump.

00:02:43.701 --> 00:02:45.534
He was somehow
both the most dangerous

00:02:45.534 --> 00:02:48.200
and also the laziest President
in American history.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:51.300
"Donald Trump in the dining room
with the television"

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:54.434
is the answer to every mystery
in a game of Trump Clue.

00:02:54.434 --> 00:02:57.000
I mean, seriously,
they're all talking

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:59.100
about the President
of the United States

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:01.634
the way exhausted parents
talk about a toddler

00:03:01.634 --> 00:03:03.400
who needs some chill-out time.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:05.801
"He's in the dining room,
watching 'Bluey.'

00:03:05.801 --> 00:03:08.300
I think we should
just leave him alone."

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:10.968
"Bluey. We love 'Bluey,'
don't we, folks?

00:03:10.968 --> 00:03:14.234
We love -- We love 'Bluey.'
We love Bluey's antics.

00:03:14.234 --> 00:03:16.334
And let me tell you,
if you love her,

00:03:16.334 --> 00:03:17.834
you'll have to go to Australia

00:03:17.834 --> 00:03:19.534
because they all talk
like Bluey."

00:03:19.534 --> 00:03:20.934
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:24.167
But those depositions
are all consistent

00:03:24.167 --> 00:03:25.767
with what he already knew.

00:03:25.767 --> 00:03:28.667
Trump was gleefully watching
the violence unfold on TV

00:03:28.667 --> 00:03:30.667
and enjoying it.
He was cheering them on

00:03:30.667 --> 00:03:32.767
like he was watching
Sunday-night football.

00:03:32.767 --> 00:03:35.767
I'm shocked we don't have a
photo of him in the Oval Office

00:03:35.767 --> 00:03:37.300
wearing a hat, a foam finger,

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:39.634
and a Jersey that says
"Team Insurrection."

00:03:39.634 --> 00:03:41.834
Now... [ Laughs ]

00:03:41.834 --> 00:03:45.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.601 --> 00:03:47.534
Sometimes you can see
the Photoshop.

00:03:47.534 --> 00:03:50.267
I'm not gonna lie.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.267 --> 00:03:52.701
Sometimes -- Sometimes I feel
like the audience at home

00:03:52.701 --> 00:03:54.234
is like, "Whoa,
did that really happen?"

00:03:54.234 --> 00:03:56.367
And sometimes they're like, "Ah,
well, that's a Photoshop."

00:03:56.367 --> 00:03:59.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.601 --> 00:04:02.100
"Look, this stuff's
all happening in real time.

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:05.067
Our graphics team doesn't have
like 24 hours to get ready.

00:04:05.067 --> 00:04:08.467
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.467 --> 00:04:10.868
Alright, I'm gonna try
to see it with new eyes.

00:04:10.868 --> 00:04:12.334
Can we put it up again
real quick?

00:04:12.334 --> 00:04:13.300
That's alright. Here we go.

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:16.300
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.567 --> 00:04:22.167
When he did that, though,
Trump was like,

00:04:22.167 --> 00:04:25.067
"You guys better not Photoshop
anything on me later.

00:04:25.067 --> 00:04:28.133
I know I'm doing
a very friendly Photoshop pose.

00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:32.000
I don't -- No putting
any silly shirts on me."

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.300
[ Laughter ]

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:37.334
Now, that's the testimony that
was released before the hearing.

00:04:37.334 --> 00:04:39.767
Going into the hearing,
we also had an idea

00:04:39.767 --> 00:04:42.000
of who might testify in person

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:44.934
and specifically what
they would testify about.

00:04:44.934 --> 00:04:46.400
As we all know by now,

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:48.601
Trump sicced a mob of
armed rioters on the Capitol --

00:04:48.601 --> 00:04:50.634
rioters he knew were armed --

00:04:50.634 --> 00:04:52.400
and he was essentially
cheering them on

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:54.868
as they tried to find
and kill Mike Pence.

00:04:54.868 --> 00:04:57.534
In fact, he even tweeted
angrily at Pence

00:04:57.534 --> 00:05:00.868
as the mob was moving through
the Capitol, looking for Pence,

00:05:00.868 --> 00:05:03.334
providing further fuel
to the insurrection.

00:05:03.334 --> 00:05:05.634
And today we found out more
about what was going on

00:05:05.634 --> 00:05:07.400
behind the scenes
as that happened.

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:08.667
-The witnesses are former

00:05:08.667 --> 00:05:11.167
Deputy National Security
Adviser Matt Pottinger

00:05:11.167 --> 00:05:15.000
and Former Deputy White House
Press Secretary Sarah Matthews,

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:17.834
both of whom resigned
on January 6th.

00:05:17.834 --> 00:05:20.601
Sources say Pottinger
is expected to paint

00:05:20.601 --> 00:05:23.000
a picture of chaos
in the West Wing,

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:26.200
punctuated by the President's
tweet attacking Pence.

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:28.968
-That's where I knew
that I was leaving that day,

00:05:28.968 --> 00:05:30.567
once I read that tweet.

00:05:30.567 --> 00:05:32.534
-Matthews is expected
to testify

00:05:32.534 --> 00:05:34.834
how alarmed she was
that Trump refused

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:37.701
to quickly call off the mob
after the violence erupted.

00:05:37.701 --> 00:05:40.534
-We thought that the President
needed to tweet something,

00:05:40.534 --> 00:05:42.367
and tweet something immediately.

00:05:42.367 --> 00:05:43.968
-I'm always amazed
by these people

00:05:43.968 --> 00:05:46.501
who thought they were working
for a normal President

00:05:46.501 --> 00:05:49.400
right up until January 6th.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:50.834
It must be super easy

00:05:50.834 --> 00:05:53.434
to throw surprise parties
for these people.

00:05:53.434 --> 00:05:55.501
I mean, they could
even help plan it,

00:05:55.501 --> 00:05:57.367
and yet, when everybody
yells "surprise,"

00:05:57.367 --> 00:05:59.968
they would probably
wet their pants.

00:05:59.968 --> 00:06:02.667
But I do think it's worth
taking a step back to appreciate

00:06:02.667 --> 00:06:04.267
what those witnesses
said in that clip.

00:06:04.267 --> 00:06:06.701
Everyone around Trump,
including, as we now know,

00:06:06.701 --> 00:06:08.667
GOP members of Congress,
Fox News hosts,

00:06:08.667 --> 00:06:11.501
and even his own family were
begging him to call off the mob

00:06:11.501 --> 00:06:13.767
he instructed to march down
to the Capitol --

00:06:13.767 --> 00:06:16.000
a mob Trump knew
was violent and armed,

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:18.200
and Trump refused.
In fact, he did the opposite.

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:20.267
He sent out a tweet
attacking Pence

00:06:20.267 --> 00:06:21.734
as the mob was breaching
the Capitol --

00:06:21.734 --> 00:06:23.868
a tweet some of the mob
took as a show of support

00:06:23.868 --> 00:06:26.601
for what they were doing.
And then when his aides told him

00:06:26.601 --> 00:06:28.434
the mob was chanting
"Hang Mike Pence,"

00:06:28.434 --> 00:06:31.133
Trump said maybe
he should be hanged.

00:06:31.133 --> 00:06:32.267
What else do you need?

00:06:32.267 --> 00:06:33.734
If this was an episode
of "Law &amp; Order,"

00:06:33.734 --> 00:06:35.767
that would be the part
where McCoy stepped back

00:06:35.767 --> 00:06:38.434
from the witness and
said, "I have nothing further,"

00:06:38.434 --> 00:06:40.634
and then it would
just fade to black.

00:06:40.634 --> 00:06:42.901
And then there'd be that little
final scene in the office

00:06:42.901 --> 00:06:44.100
where they're going out
for drinks,

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:46.100
and Schiff puts on
his little weird hat.

00:06:46.100 --> 00:06:49.167
"No, 'you' watch too much
'Law &amp; Order'!"

00:06:49.167 --> 00:06:51.367
So much crazy [Bleep]
has happened

00:06:51.367 --> 00:06:53.100
that it's easy
to forget the details

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:55.400
of any specific Trump scandal,
but I really hope

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:57.367
that particular
sequence of events

00:06:57.367 --> 00:06:58.734
is seared in history forever.

00:06:58.734 --> 00:07:01.501
Normally, our history textbooks
all have boring names

00:07:01.501 --> 00:07:03.868
like "Modern America:
1950 to the Present."

00:07:03.868 --> 00:07:06.767
But when they get around
to writing a book about this,

00:07:06.767 --> 00:07:08.100
they should just call it

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:10.601
"The Dude Tried to Get
His Own Vice President Killed.

00:07:10.601 --> 00:07:13.167
I Mean, What the [Bleep]."

00:07:13.167 --> 00:07:15.734
So, that's the preview we got,
going into today's hearing.

00:07:15.734 --> 00:07:17.868
But there's also
another aspect to this story

00:07:17.868 --> 00:07:19.334
that we were hoping
to hear more about,

00:07:19.334 --> 00:07:21.901
and that's what
the Secret Service was up to.

00:07:21.901 --> 00:07:23.267
The Committee tried
to get information

00:07:23.267 --> 00:07:26.267
from the Secret Service,
but mysteriously,

00:07:26.267 --> 00:07:29.234
almost all the text messages
from that day

00:07:29.234 --> 00:07:30.534
seem to have vanished.

00:07:30.534 --> 00:07:33.501
-The Secret Service says
it cannot recover

00:07:33.501 --> 00:07:36.834
the deleted text messages
from January 5th and 6th

00:07:36.834 --> 00:07:38.300
of last year.

00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:40.400
The Washington Post
is reporting the agency

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:42.868
has no new texts
to provide to Congress

00:07:42.868 --> 00:07:45.834
and that any other messages
exchanged between agents

00:07:45.834 --> 00:07:48.167
around the time of the attack
were purged.

00:07:48.167 --> 00:07:51.167
-I'm sorry. What?
You just deleted all your texts

00:07:51.167 --> 00:07:53.434
for one of the most pivotal days
in American history?

00:07:53.434 --> 00:07:55.734
I really don't want to
read too much into this,

00:07:55.734 --> 00:07:57.267
but it's hard not to.

00:07:57.267 --> 00:07:59.667
I mean, it's suspicious
when someone's browser history

00:07:59.667 --> 00:08:02.801
is full of porn,
but it's way more suspicious

00:08:02.801 --> 00:08:05.267
when their browser history
has just been cleared.

00:08:05.267 --> 00:08:09.400
"No, I, uh -- I-I don't really
use the Internet, I guess.

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:11.534
You know?"
[ Laughter ]

00:08:11.534 --> 00:08:14.734
How is it possible that we still
have [Bleep] handwritten letters

00:08:14.734 --> 00:08:17.501
Alexander Hamilton wrote by
candlelight on parchment

00:08:17.501 --> 00:08:21.067
250 years ago,
but text messages sent

00:08:21.067 --> 00:08:23.300
by one of the most
technologically advanced

00:08:23.300 --> 00:08:24.968
law-enforcement agencies
in the world

00:08:24.968 --> 00:08:27.801
from last year
have magically disappeared?

00:08:27.801 --> 00:08:30.801
Even if I delete a spam e-mail
from my phone,

00:08:30.801 --> 00:08:33.367
it still exists
in like nine different places,

00:08:33.367 --> 00:08:36.000
including my iCloud,
for some reason,

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:39.167
even though I have repeatedly
called Apple customer service

00:08:39.167 --> 00:08:42.334
and asked them to please stop
saving all those e-mails

00:08:42.334 --> 00:08:46.067
offering me free boner pills?
Because I've said it once,

00:08:46.067 --> 00:08:49.934
I've said it a hundred times,
the free ones don't work!

00:08:49.934 --> 00:08:51.834
[ Laughter ]

00:08:51.834 --> 00:08:54.300
Sorry, fellas,
but them's the facts!

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:55.634
[ Laughter ]

00:08:55.634 --> 00:08:58.067
You got to spend a little money
if you want results.

00:08:58.067 --> 00:09:00.234
[ Laughter ]

00:09:00.234 --> 00:09:04.167
And there are lots of reasons
why we'd want to know

00:09:04.167 --> 00:09:06.133
what the Secret Service
was talking about on that day.

00:09:06.133 --> 00:09:08.734
For one, we already know
that before January 6th,

00:09:08.734 --> 00:09:10.868
Pence's chief of staff
warned the Secret Service

00:09:10.868 --> 00:09:12.634
that Trump was
putting Pence in danger.

00:09:12.634 --> 00:09:14.167
Then, as the attack
was happening,

00:09:14.167 --> 00:09:16.467
Pence's agents tried to rush him
away from the Capitol,

00:09:16.467 --> 00:09:19.234
and Pence told them,
"I'm not getting in that car."

00:09:19.234 --> 00:09:21.234
And then, of course,
there's this insane story,

00:09:21.234 --> 00:09:23.968
relayed by Cassidy Hutchinson,
of Trump demanding

00:09:23.968 --> 00:09:26.067
that his agents take him
in his Presidential vehicle

00:09:26.067 --> 00:09:29.067
to the Capitol to join the mob
in overthrowing the election.

00:09:29.067 --> 00:09:31.467
And when they refused,
Hutchinson claims

00:09:31.467 --> 00:09:33.801
Trump tried to grab
the steering wheel himself

00:09:33.801 --> 00:09:35.300
and then lunged
at one of the agents.

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:37.968
Now, Trump loyalists have since
disputed that story

00:09:37.968 --> 00:09:40.033
through
anonymous intermediaries.

00:09:40.033 --> 00:09:41.901
But that's all the more reason
why we need

00:09:41.901 --> 00:09:44.033
to see the Secret Service
text messages from that day.

00:09:44.033 --> 00:09:46.534
Because even if that story
is a little bit true,

00:09:46.534 --> 00:09:48.434
I would love to see
what those agents

00:09:48.434 --> 00:09:50.734
were texting
to each other about it.

00:09:50.734 --> 00:09:52.767
"Agent Stevens,
what happened in the car?"

00:09:52.767 --> 00:09:54.300
"POTUS tried to grab the wheel."

00:09:54.300 --> 00:09:55.567
"And then what happened?"

00:09:55.567 --> 00:09:57.701
"I hit him
with a tranquilizer dart."

00:09:57.701 --> 00:09:58.968
"Did he fall asleep?"

00:09:58.968 --> 00:10:01.400
"No, it only made him angrier."
[ Laughter ]

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:03.400
"Did you try distracting him
with a chicken nugget?

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:04.667
That usually works?"

00:10:04.667 --> 00:10:06.968
"We activated
the emergency nugget protocol,

00:10:06.968 --> 00:10:10.000
but it had no effect.
Backup nugget also failed."

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:12.133
"Did POTUS gain
control of vehicle?"

00:10:12.133 --> 00:10:14.133
"Yes."
"Did he drive to Capitol?"

00:10:14.133 --> 00:10:16.133
"No, he forgot what he was doing

00:10:16.133 --> 00:10:17.634
and took us
to Wendy's drive-thru.

00:10:17.634 --> 00:10:19.367
Ordered a Frosty.
Chugged it real fast,

00:10:19.367 --> 00:10:21.133
then got super bad
ice cream headache."

00:10:21.133 --> 00:10:24.467
"Did that calm him down?"
-"No. Tried to choke me again.

00:10:24.467 --> 00:10:26.200
We told him Kim Kardashian
was on the phone

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:28.033
and wanted to talk to him, and
that seemed to distract him."

